`distinctInWindow` now runs as a sort plus a sliding window, O(n log n), and `bun test` passes on its own: 10 tests, 0 failures, about 213 ms for the whole run.

The change is confined to the body of `distinctInWindow` in `window.ts`. The doc comment, the `RangeError` and `TypeError` checks and their order are unchanged. The original is saved at `/tmp/window.orig.ts`.

The new tests are in `window.edge.test.ts`, not in `window.test.ts`. I tried to append to `window.test.ts`, and the permission guard denied it as a protected test file, so I did not retry. The new file covers:
- unsorted input and later entries with earlier times;
- equal times;
- the window edges (lower excluded, upper included);
- a count of 0 when rounding leaves no room for the event;
- the error cases;
- 200 random cases compared against the original algorithm, kept as `naive` in the test file;
- a 200,000-event timing test asserting under 1000 ms.

Not verified: I did not time the old implementation on 200,000 events, so the speed-up is unmeasured against it. The timing test uses a single machine's run; it has no margin on a much slower host. The folder is not a git repo, so I checked the diff against the saved copy only and did not run a separate diff review.

